node_modules/
dist/
# Templates are tracked (`.env`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, `.env.test-*`); the values
# that belong to one machine or one deployment are not. Both the app's loader and docker-compose read
# a `.local` file on top of the template it names, so a secret only ever lives there — and the
# `.env.production` template's placeholders are what a deployment overrides.
.env.local
.env.*.local
rush-logs/
*.tsbuildinfo
# The container's log directory is a compose bind mount: the directory itself is tracked (so the
# mount target exists with sane ownership), what lands in it is not.
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
